      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2024 the Syndicate's gross claims outstanding were $3,416.9m. During 2024 the Syndicate recorded a net release in prior year claims estimates; the claims provisions note shows a gross reduction in prior year provisions of $25.782m (a circa 0.75% release of opening gross claims outstanding). Management attributes the favourable movement predominantly to favourable claims development on prior year losses, partly offset by reserve strengthening related to Political Risk/Violence and exposures arising from the Russia/Ukraine crisis and other large man-made losses. Material named events cited in the reserves note for 2024 include Dubai flooding, Hurricanes Helene and Milton, Typhoon Yagi, Calgary hailstorms and the Baltimore bridge collapse, with quantified gross estimates provided for some events.",
